<!--
  Commander Battle's Battanian troop classes, merged into Native's mpclassdivisions.xml (MPClassDivisions, MultiplayerGame
  only). Same rules as cb_mpclassdivisions_vlandia.xml:
  - One class per weight of a formation class (role). The weight label comes from the multiplier bands
    (CommanderRoles.WeightBands), so each multiplier stays inside its band.
  - Battania has exactly 7 classes, so all of them take over the 7 stock class ids in place (_replaceWhileMerging="true")
    and keep the stock index (MissionPeer.SelectedTroopIndex). There are no new class ids. Never put
    _replaceWhileMerging on a NEW id: with no id match the merger replaces the FIRST class of the file instead
    (MBObjectManager.MergeElements).
  - A stock id's role comes only from its hero's default_group, so mp_skirmisher_battania becomes the medium cavalry
    (the culture's only leftover id once the three infantry, two ranged and light cavalry weights have theirs).
  - multiplier: the class's size weight. A formation fields budget x ceil(100 x multiplier) / the average of its role's
    classes, so it only compares within a role.
  - The only perk list (perk_list="1") is the weapon setups. Index 0 is the class's own loadout; the others swap weapon
    slots with AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn (commander and troops). No TroopCountOnSpawn: only the weight sets the
    count. game_mode="all": the server's GameType is CommanderBattle, so stock "Captain" perks would never apply.
    AI-led formations get a setup too (MissionMultiplayerCommanderBattle.AssignDefaultClasses), picked by index, so
    every weight of a role lists the role's setups in the plan's order (docs/plans/troop-types.md, culture variance
    pass): infantry spear + round shield, pike, sword or axe + big round shield, falx, skirmisher; ranged longbow +
    two-handed sidearm, heavy longbow; cavalry spear + big round shield, mounted skirmisher.
  - Battania: the best longbows, javelin skirmishers, pikes and falxes, the fastest infantry. No heavy cavalry and the
    lightest heavy infantry: the armour sits a step below Vlandia and Sturgia at each weight.
  - Setups without a shield (pike, falx) clear the shield slot (Item1: an AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn without item sets
    an empty element, AlternativeEquipmentEffect.Deserialize). Throwing weapons only in the skirmisher setups. The
    heavy longbow trades the two-handed sidearm for a one-handed one.
  - Sidearm (Item2) rule: spears, pikes, lances and javelins keep the culture's sword, since they fight poorly up
    close. Swords and axes, and swung two-handers (falx, rhomphaia), clear it: their main weapon already is one.
  - A bad node makes the loader drop every later entry of this file silently; the CommanderBattle log lists the
    classes per culture when a mission opens.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml (the only items multiplayer loads).
-->
